<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Sentlog SDK privacy manifest.

      The SDK itself collects nothing. It runs entirely on-device and
      transmits no data unless the integrator explicitly configures a
      forwarder (see SentlogConfig.forwarders). When forwarders are
      configured, the integrator's app is the data controller and is
      responsible for declaring the collection in its own privacy
      manifest.

      Three runtime permissions are required depending on the config:

        - Microphone (always, for the voice pipeline). Declare
          NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in the integrator's Info.plist.
        - Motion (when SentlogConfig.useMotionSensors == true, for
          presence.motion in Phase 3c). CoreMotion does not require
          a usage-description string on iOS but the access is logged
          by the OS; declare NSMotionUsageDescription if your app
          chooses to surface it.
        - Camera (when SentlogConfig.useVideoAffect == true, for
          the affect block in Phase 5). Declare
          NSCameraUsageDescription in the integrator's Info.plist.
          Camera frames never leave the device under any projection
          (spec §5.3) — only derived (valence, arousal, FAU) values
          reach forwarders.

      The SDK does NOT request any of these permissions itself. The
      integrator's app drives the permission prompt; if denied,
      sentlog_start_capture returns SENTLOG_ERR_PERMISSION_DENIED
      via the binding's typed error.
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array/>
</dict>
</plist>
